laprust 1.0.0 is derived from the lapjvr solver family of LAPX 0.11.1
(rathaROG/lapx, v0.11.1).

The square Jonker-Volgenant implementation derives from source{d}/lapjv
and carries the copyright of Vadim Markovtsev (2016). Native rectangular
assignment, implicit rejection handling, adapters and batch execution derive
from Ratha SIV's LAPX work (2026). See src/_lapjv/LICENSE for the full MIT text.
The top-level LICENSE covers this package. Neither package requires LAPX.

Rust dependencies and their notices are listed in src/_lapjv/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.

Historical regression matrices and fixture generators are adapted from LAPX/gatagat-lap tests under BSD-2-Clause. See tests/LICENSE. The epsilon dataset was contributed by Michael Lewis.
